/Title (Our results showed that traditional models like SVM and XGBoost performed very well with sparse representations like TF-IDF and Bag of Words. However, the best overall performance was achieved using Word2Vec embeddings with a Bidirectional LSTM model. This combination captured deeper semantic and contextual meaning, making it more effective for classifying sentiment in dialectal Arabic.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1380 0 R
/Next 1479 0 R
>>
endobj
1479 0 obj
<<
/Title (In the end, this study not only highlights the potential of deep learning with semantic embeddings for Arabic sentiment analysis, but also emphasizes the importance of choosing the right feature representation and model combination.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1380 0 R
/Prev 1478 0 R
